      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good point, we should consider the boost margin.\n\nBut I think if we only consider task boost margin is not enough, we need to consider boost margin for both CPU\u0027s existed boost margin and the waken task\u0027s boost margin together.\n\nSo I suggest the function group_max_util() should firstly check the max boost margin from CPU level and task level, then use the boost margin to inflate the \u0027util\u0027 value; so finally group_max_util() will return back the maximum util value with boost margin applied. Then find_best_target() can directly select a capacity index for this.\n\nDoes this idea make sense for you?",
